From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: report window title changes to WinEvent hooks in the external shell

Purpose: let the bridge proxy follow Win32 window titles without polling.
XP behavior: DefWindowProc's WM_SETTEXT raises EVENT_OBJECT_NAMECHANGE, and
out-of-context WinEvent hooks receive it.
Wine before: Wine 10 raised create, destroy, show, hide, foreground and
minimize events but not this one, so the proxy re-read every title five
times a second to send the taskbar HSHELL_REDRAW.
Change: raise the event after DefWindowProc stores a new title.
Evidence: tests/bridge_integration.py checks that a title change reaches
the proxy.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL.
Old patches: 0073.
---
 dlls/win32u/defwnd.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
index 7f5d0a4..cfdadd2 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/defwnd.c
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #include "ntgdi_private.h"
 #include "ntuser_private.h"
 #include "wine/server.h"
+#include "wine/win4wine.h"
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(win);
 
@@ -2613,6 +2614,10 @@ LRESULT default_window_proc( HWND hwnd, UINT msg, WPARAM wparam, LPARAM lparam,
         result = set_window_text( hwnd, (void *)lparam, ansi );
         if (result && (get_window_long( hwnd, GWL_STYLE ) & WS_CAPTION) == WS_CAPTION)
             handle_nc_paint( hwnd , (HRGN)1 );  /* repaint caption */
+        /* Windows reports the new name to WinEvent hooks. The external
+         * shell's task list follows window titles through this event. */
+        if (result && win4wine_external_shell())
+            NtUserNotifyWinEvent( EVENT_OBJECT_NAMECHANGE, hwnd, OBJID_WINDOW, CHILDID_SELF );
         break;
 
     case WM_GETTEXTLENGTH:
